  "object": "text_completion",
  "created": 1754447246,
  "model": "DeepSeekR1-Qwen-32B",
  "choices": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "1980.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **99** and **20**, follow these easy steps:\n\n1. **Multiply 99 by 20:**\n   \n   \\[\n   99 \\times 20\n   \\]\n\n2. **Break down the multiplication for simplicity:**\n   \n   \\[\n   99 \\times 20 = (100 - 1) \\times 20\n   \\]\n\n3. **Apply the distributive property:**\n   \n   \\[\n   = 100 \\times 20 - 1 \\times 20\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate each part:**\n   \n   \\[\n   = 2000 - 20\n   \\]\n\n5. **Subtract to find the final result:**\n   \n   \\[\n   = 1980\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1980}\n\\]",
      "logprobs": null,
