      "index": 0,
      "text": "4230 + 282 = 4512.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **47** and **96**, follow these easy steps:\n\n1. **Break Down the Numbers:**\n   \n   \\[\n   96 = 90 + 6\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 47 by Each Part:**\n   \n   - **Multiply 47 by 90:**\n     \n     \\[\n     47 \\times 90 = 47 \\times 9 \\times 10 = 423 \\times 10 = 4230\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Multiply 47 by 6:**\n     \n     \\[\n     47 \\times 6 = 282\n     \\]\n\n3. **Add the Results Together:**\n   \n   \\[\n   4230 + 282 = 4512\n   \\]\n\n4. **Final Answer:**\n   \n   \\[\n   \\boxed{4512}\n   \\]",
