  "model": "DeepSeekR1-Qwen-32B",
  "choices": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "3,200 plus 640 equals 3,840.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **48** and **80**, follow these easy steps:\n\n1. **Multiply 48 by 80:**\n   \n   \\[\n   48 \\times 80\n   \\]\n\n2. **Break down the multiplication for simplicity:**\n   \n   \\[\n   48 \\times 80 = (40 + 8) \\times 80\n   \\]\n   \n3. **Apply the distributive property:**\n   \n   \\[\n   = 40 \\times 80 + 8 \\times 80\n   \\]\n   \n4. **Calculate each part:**\n   \n   \\[\n   40 \\times 80 = 3,\\!200\n   \\]\n   \n   \\[\n   8 \\times 80 = 640\n   \\]\n   \n5. **Add the results together:**\n   \n   \\[\n   3,\\!200 + 640 = 3,\\!840\n   \\]\n   \n6. **Final Answer:**\n   \n   \\[\n   \\boxed{3,\\!840}\n   \\]",
      "logprobs": null,
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "stop_reason": null,
      "prompt_logprobs": null
    }
  ],
