      "index": 0,
      "text": "936.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 26 and 36, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Multiply 26 by 36:**\n\n   \\[\n   26 \\times 36\n   \\]\n\n2. **Break down the multiplication:**\n\n   \\[\n   26 \\times 36 = (20 + 6) \\times 36\n   \\]\n\n3. **Apply the distributive property:**\n\n   \\[\n   = 20 \\times 36 + 6 \\times 36\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate each part:**\n\n   \\[\n   20 \\times 36 = 720\n   \\]\n   \n   \\[\n   6 \\times 36 = 216\n   \\]\n\n5. **Add the results together:**\n\n   \\[\n   720 + 216 = 936\n   \\]\n\n6. **Final Answer:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{936}\n   \\]",
      "logprobs": null,
