  "object": "text_completion",
  "created": 1754448025,
  "model": "DeepSeekR1-Qwen-32B",
  "choices": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "6,660 plus 444 equals 7,104.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **74** and **96**, follow these easy steps:\n\n1. **Multiply 74 by 96:**\n\n   \\[\n   74 \\times 96\n   \\]\n\n2. **Break down the multiplication for simplicity:**\n\n   \\[\n   74 \\times 96 = 74 \\times (90 + 6) = (74 \\times 90) + (74 \\times 6)\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate each part separately:**\n\n   - **First part:**\n     \n     \\[\n     74 \\times 90 = 6,660\n     \\]\n     \n     *(Because \\(74 \\times 9 = 666\\) and \\(666 \\times 10 = 6,660\\).)*\n\n   - **Second part:**\n     \n     \\[\n     74 \\times 6 = 444\n     \\]\n\n4. **Add the two results together:**\n\n   \\[\n   6,660 + 444 = 7,104\n   \\]\n\n5. **Final Answer:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{7,\\!104}\n   \\]",
      "logprobs": null,
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "stop_reason": null,
